SECTION 3 — PHISHING & SOCIAL ENGINEERING ANALYSIS

Task 1 — Phishing Indicator Analysis (at least 5)


Phishing Indicator
Analytical Explanation (Why It’s Suspicious)
1.Sender domain mismatch
Email claims to be from “IT Support” but uses it-support@aitee-care-security.com. Legitimate organizational domain is aitee-care.org. Evidence suggests domain spoofing / look-alike domain.
2.Urgency language + time pressure
Subject “ACTION REQUIRED” and body text “verify their account within 30 minutes. Failure… may result in temporary account suspension” creates artificial deadline.
3.Generic greeting + broad targeting
Addressed to “Administrative Staff” rather than a named individual, typical of bulk spear-phishing
4.Call-to-action link only
Sole interactive element is a hyperlinked “VERIFY ACCOUNT” button with no legitimate verification process described.
5.Unexpected MFA push after credential entry
User received an unsolicited MFA prompt immediately after submitting credentials on the linked page; user later confirmed the 10:05 AM login was not intentional






Task 2 — Social Engineering Psychological Analysis(at least 2)



Technique
Psychological Mechanism & Operational Impact
1.Technique 1: Urgency / Fear of loss
Threat of account suspension within 30 minutes exploits fear of operational disruption. This pressured the employee to click the link and enter credentials without verification.
2.Technique 2: Authority / Trust
Email is framed as originating from the internal “IT Security Team.” Users are conditioned to comply with IT directives, lowering scrutiny of the domain and link.







